    <comment>New package: rtk 0.44.2 (Rust Token Killer)

Command line proxy for the shell commands coding agents run most often. It
executes the wrapped command, filters and compresses the output, and prints
only the informative part, cutting the tokens the result costs in an LLM
context window. Ships filters for build systems, linters, test runners,
version control and cloud tooling, and passes unrecognised commands through
unchanged.

Apache-2.0, single Rust binary, upstream https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk

Two downstream patches, both submitted upstream:
- rtk-unbundle-sqlite.patch links the system SQLite instead of the copy
  statically linked in from libsqlite3-sys, so the binary is covered by the
  distribution SQLite updates (upstream PR 3446).
- rtk-no-deny-warnings.patch stops rustc warnings being promoted to errors;
  the distribution rustc moves independently of the version floor upstream
  builds against (upstream PR 3447).

Telemetry is opt-in only and stays off unless explicitly enabled.

Verified on aarch64 (local) and x86_64 (OBS): builds green, test suite
2584 passed / 0 failed, rpmlint 0 errors 0 warnings 0 badness.</comment>
